cd /workspaces/mapan-journeyFrom 4661d9b9f8add2f836938491bd5be54debdf33c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 06:09:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Remove backup/restore (redundant with cloud sync), add
 facilitator role gating

- store.js: removed backup() and restore() entirely -- now that Supabase
  syncs everyone's state automatically on login, a manual JSON
  export/import is redundant, and importing an outdated backup file
  could silently overwrite newer cloud-synced data.
- store.js: on session, ensures a mapan_profiles row exists for the user
  (defaults to role='participant') and reads back their actual role.
- Profil.jsx: Backup Data / Pulihkan Data buttons removed; Dashboard
  Fasilitator button now only shows when role === 'facilitator'.
- Dashboard.jsx: added a role check at the top of the component itself
  (not just hiding the button) -- shows 'Halaman ini khusus fasilitator.'
  and skips the data fetch entirely for non-facilitators.
- Supabase migration: added role column to mapan_profiles (default
  'participant'); marked vzhar.akbar@gmail.com as 'facilitator'; replaced
  the mapan_checkin_results SELECT policy so only rows from a user whose
  profile role is 'facilitator' can read it -- real DB-level enforcement,
  not just a hidden UI button.
